NNAAMMEE
     uuiippaaqq — USB support for iPAQ units

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee uuccoomm
           ddeevviiccee uuiippaaqq

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           uipaq_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuiippaaqq driver provides support for the USB serial emulation provided
     by the iPAQ devices.

     The device is accessed through the ucom(4) driver which makes it behave
     like a tty(4).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The uuiippaaqq driver supports the following iPAQ devices:

     ••   ASUS P535 PDA
     ••   Casio BE300 PDA
     ••   Compaq IPaq PocketPC
     ••   HP Jornada 568
     ••   HP iPAQ 22xx/Jornada 548
     ••   HTC PPC6700 Modem
     ••   HTC Smart Phone
     ••   HTC Winmobile
     ••   Sharp W-ZERO3 ES Spart Phone
     ••   Most Windows CE based phones

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/ttyU*       for callin ports
     /dev/ttyU*.init
     /dev/ttyU*.lock  corresponding callin initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

     /dev/cuaU*       for callout ports
     /dev/cuaU*.init
     /dev/cuaU*.lock  corresponding callout initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     tty(4), ucom(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The FreeBSD support was imported from NetBSD for FreeBSD 7.0.  NetBSD
     added support in NetBSD 4.0 and it was imported from OpenBSD 3.8.

